WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.740
- We've said it a million times,

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:02.850
but it bears repeating,

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.670
money is not just numbers and math.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.790
A dollar bill doesn't
have any value in itself.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:11.010
It's a symbol of human values.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:14.490
What we want, who we trust,
what our priorities are,

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.740
how you decide to spend it or save it

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.350
can be a window into
your hopes and dreams,

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.110
but also your fears and traumas.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:26.220
- The point is money is
intrinsically emotional.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.410
We can try to be as rational as possible

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.150
when making financial decisions,

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.820
but your brain is not a spreadsheet.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.950
Besides, good financial decisions

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.320
should take your emotions into account.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.730
What would be the point of money

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.410
if it couldn't make you happy?

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:41.940
- But, sometimes, our emotions

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.250
can hijack our financial decision making

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.430
in a way that is recurring
and self destructive.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:49.290
- When someone slips into such a pattern,

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:51.630
it's known as a money disorder.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.190
There are many different types

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.290
with different causes
and negative impacts.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:59.500
- You might recognize one in
someone you know or yourself.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.083
(upbeat music)

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:09.810
- In their book, Mind Over Money,

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.510
financial psychologists
Brad and Ted Klontz

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:16.080
divided money disorders
into three main categories,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.540
money avoidance, money worship,

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.580
and relational money disorders.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.680
Money avoidance refers to people who,

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.180
for one reason or another,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.081
are made very uncomfortable
by the idea of money

00:01:27.081 --> 00:01:31.110
and go to dangerous lengths
to escape the topic.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.440
The most common type is financial denial,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.440
often spurred by income
loss, overwhelming debt,

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.450
or other financial woes.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.430
Those suffering from financial denial

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.550
avoid all reminders of
their money problems.

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:47.550
This can mean never checking
their account balances,

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.440
ignoring credit card statements,

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.440
and, in extreme cases, neglecting bills

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.510
or not filing their taxes.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:57.150
- Obviously, you can
only pretend for so long.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.490
Eventually, reality will assert itself

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.410
and the longer you've had
your head in the sand,

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.390
the worse the consequences will be.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.850
A bad credit score is the
least of your worries.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.790
You could go bankrupt,
get audited, even evicted.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:11.070
In trying to avoid the emotional pain

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:12.480
of facing your money problems,

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.870
you've just made those
problems much, much worse.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:16.710
- A less common

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:19.200
but still damaging form
of money avoidance

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.930
is known as financial rejection.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.090
If someone has low self-esteem,

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:27.060
gaining money can
trigger feelings of guilt

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.410
and worthlessness.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.660
They may deliberately avoid steps

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.300
that most of us would
consider financially smart,

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:36.900
like asking for a raise or
making long term investments.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:40.230
They may also give their
money away to family, friends,

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.640
or strangers.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.010
- That doesn't sound so bad, noble even.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.010
After all, many of our
cultural and spiritual heroes

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.870
rejected the pursuit of money.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.240
- Sure, if you make a conscious choice

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.420
to give all your possessions
away and live a monastic life,

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.240
we're not gonna say that's
not a valid life choice,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.580
but if you're doing it out of compulsion

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.670
to avoid negative emotions about yourself,

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:03.990
that may be a disorder.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.280
- And, you may put your

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.350
and your family's financial wellbeing

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:09.900
in serious jeopardy along the way.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.930
- On the other end of the
spectrum is money worship,

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:15.330
which describes people who rely on money

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.210
to alleviate emotional pain or anxiety.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:21.270
For example, most of us
have occasionally spent

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.830
a little more than we intended

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.170
or bought something we regretted,

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:28.650
but compulsive shoppers
use the act of purchasing

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.170
as a temporary relief from feelings

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.000
of depression or anxiety.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.820
- It may feel great when the
credit card is being swiped,

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.560
but once the shopping spree is over

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.180
and you're back home with all the stuff

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.890
you know you'll never use,

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:44.340
the negative emotions set back
in, even worse than before,

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.860
with a hefty credit card bill to boot.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:50.220
- Compulsive gambling is one
of the few money disorders

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.538
officially recognized

00:03:51.538 --> 00:03:55.140
by the American Psychiatric
Association Diagnostic

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:56.910
and Statistical Manual.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:04:00.060
And, it doesn't just happen at
the casino or the racetrack.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:03.180
An addiction to the risk
reward dopamine cycle

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:06.870
can be gratified by lottery
tickets, stock trading,

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.360
even video game loot boxes.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:10.770
For compulsive gamblers,

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.770
the thrill of winning is so intoxicating

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.240
that they're even willing to risk

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.190
their family's livelihood for it.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.980
And the pain of losing is so great

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.320
that the only thing that can alleviate it

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.350
is to chase the high of winning again.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:27.420
- Earning and saving
are generally considered

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.250
to be positive financial behaviors,

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.830
but even they can be taken too far.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.680
Workaholics get so anxious
when they're not working

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.840
that they can't enjoy
their hobbies, vacations,

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.460
or time spent with family.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.580
And hoarders are so intent
on building their money pile

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.280
that they may deprive themselves
of important life goals

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:45.540
and experiences.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.550
Again, what pushes these behaviors

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.140
into unhealthy territory

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.030
is that the activity is not pursued

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.130
for its own pleasures or benefits,

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:56.910
but as a ritual to keep
negative emotions at bay.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.850
- Lastly, there are
relational money disorders,

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:02.910
disorders that involve close
relationships with spouses,

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.560
family, and friends.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.150
Financial infidelity

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:10.230
is the act of deceiving one's
partner about money matters.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:12.960
This can mean secret spending and debts,

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.910
keeping a private bank account,

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:17.370
or even stealing from each other.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:20.730
Financial infidelity is often
related to other disorders

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:23.040
like a spouse who has to cover up debts

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.680
resulting from compulsive gambling.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.020
- Financial enabling
and financial dependency

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.850
are two sides of one coin.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.740
They refer to an unhealthy relationship

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.590
in which one person is
totally reliant on the other

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:36.750
for all their financial
needs and accounting,

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.600
even if they have the
means to be independent.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.760
This is most often seen in parents

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:43.770
who continue to support an adult child

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:45.450
who takes no responsibility

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:47.370
in their own financial situation.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:48.660
- This is not to say

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.400
that people shouldn't help each other out

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.840
during tough times.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.270
Lord knows our parents did it for us,

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:57.240
but if it's a long term recurring dynamic

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.450
in which the parent is
sacrificing their own retirement

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:02.730
for a child who is not even making a plan

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:04.140
to become independent,

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:07.800
then it may be fair to call
the relationship dysfunctional.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.030
- Another relational disorder

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:11.250
is known as financial enmeshment,

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:13.770
when a parent inappropriately or unfairly

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:17.010
involves a young child into
their financial hardship.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:18.810
This can be done to elicit sympathy,

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:21.600
to make the child feel guilty
for the costs they incur,

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:24.990
or even to demean one's
spouse in the child's eyes.

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:27.780
- If you recognize any of
these disorders in yourself

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.160
or someone close to you,

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.800
you may be wondering what
can be done about them.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:35.340
- Anything so connected to
emotions has no easy fix,

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:37.980
but there are some places to seek help.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:40.200
You can ask a spouse
or other family member

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.330
to help manage the household's money

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.370
or you can use apps that schedule

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.590
and automate payments and investments.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.170
- But that may not
free you from the trauma

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:52.770
or anxiety that causes the
disorders in the first place.

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.720
There are a lot of resources out there,

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.760
from books to podcasts,

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:58.860
to help you identify your emotions,

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:00.420
and not feel so alone.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.190
- But talking with a professional,

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.080
like a therapist or psychologist,

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.630
is often the best way to
support your financial

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:08.940
and emotional wellbeing.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.130
- [All] And that's our two cents.

